From: he_is_the_cat <125207670+heisthecat31@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Atrium: room calibration for more than one Rift sensor

Upstream put every sensor at the same placeholder pose, so with two sensors
each saw a device somewhere else and poses snapped between them. Now the
first sensor is the reference and every other one is placed as Meta's runtime
does it: from where a device (a Touch, the headset) is in moments both it and
a placed sensor see it. Each moment is a point pair (the device in this
sensor's frame, and in the origin as the placed sensor puts it); the sensor's
pose is the rigid fit of the two clouds (Horn), found among outliers with
RANSAC, refined on the agreeing points, and kept refined as more come in.
Until placed, a sensor's poses aren't used. Saved by sensor serial in
<config>/Atrium/rift_room.json, loaded at start; the Atrium app shows it.
---
